1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:02,640
Imagine working hard every single day,

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,640
earning a steady income and

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,400
remaining completely invisible

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,560
to the banking system.

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,600
In Argentina,

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,840
over 40% of the workforce

7
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,920
operates in the informal economy.

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,840
Without a formal paystub or

9
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,520
traditional credit history,

10
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,680
millions of workers and students

11
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,160
are locked out of basic financial

12
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,080
tools like credit cards.

13
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:25,520
They simply have no way

14
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,360
to pay over time.

15
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,200
We are Luciano and Ignacio,

16
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,800
and we are building Lazo,

17
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,200
a credit layer that plugs directly

18
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,520
into the fintech wallets that people

19
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,520
already use every single day.

20
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:40,160
We enable a buy now pay later

21
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:42,160
model where users can split

22
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,030
purchases into three interest-free

23
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:46,880
monthly payments or six with a

24
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,830
small interest charge.

25
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:52,800
For buyers,

26
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,040
there are three simple steps.

27
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:56,560
Pick up your product,

28
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,840
choose the installments,

29
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,550
and confirm your purchase.

30
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:01,430
For merchants, it's easy.

31
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:04,390
They get paid upfront for a small fee,

32
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:07,110
while the customer pays over time.

33
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:08,230
The money comes from a

34
00:01:08,230 --> 00:01:09,510
shared credit pool,

35
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:12,550
and every repayment fills it back up.

36
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:14,630
That pool lives on Solana.

37
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:16,790
It runs as a program that pays

38
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:18,630
merchants and collects installments

39
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:21,750
automatically by rules anyone can check.

40
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:24,390
Every loan and repayment is

41
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:25,830
recorded on chain,

42
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:27,430
and each payment flows back

43
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:29,110
into the pool in seconds,

44
00:01:29,110 --> 00:01:31,190
ready to fund the next purchase.

45
00:01:31,190 --> 00:01:32,630
We are launching our first

46
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:34,150
pilot in Argentina,

47
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:36,310
and we are looking for fintech partners

48
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:39,190
and investors to join us in scaling

49
00:01:39,190 --> 00:01:43,140
credit access across all the country.

50
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:45,630
Earning a living should be enough

51
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:47,900
to get access to credit.
